 "note": {
  "status": "draft",
  "text": "The informal sector is all the economic activities that are not registered or controlled by the State.\nExamples: street trade, bayam-sellam, call-box, motorbike taxis, tailoring at home, roadside mechanics, hairdressing, carpentry workshops, small restaurants (tourne-dos), money changers.\nCauses: unemployment, rural exodus, little education or capital needed, easy to start, the high cost and paperwork of formal businesses.\nAdvantages: it gives jobs and income to many people (especially youths and women), cheap goods and services, training (apprentices), and helps people survive.\nDisadvantages: no tax for the State, low and irregular incomes, no social security (CNPS), child labour, unsafe or dirty working places, crowded streets.\nSolutions: help informal workers to register, give them small loans, training, and organised markets.",
  "checks": []
 },
 "worked_example": {
  "status": "draft",
  "vars": {},
  "problem": "Give one advantage and one disadvantage of motorbike taxis (benskin) in towns.",
  "steps": [
   "Advantage: they give jobs to many young people and carry passengers cheaply where buses cannot go.",
   "Disadvantage: many accidents, and the drivers have no social security."
  ],
  "answer": "Jobs and cheap transport; but many accidents and no social security.",
  "checks": []
 },
